      "note": "Neumann KH 750 DSP page read 2026-11-12: \"383 x 330 x 383 mm\" (H x W x D), 19.5 kg, backplate: two electronically balanced XLR inputs, two electronically balanced XLR outputs (high-passed, a daisy chain for subwoofer arrays), one BNC input (75 ohm, AES3 or S/PDIF) and one BNC output (75 ohm, AES3), \"a standard IP network connector\" for MA 1 control, a universal switched-mode supply 100-240 V (the mains connector is not described), a 10 in long-throw woofer behind a black metal grille, sealed wood cabinet with an aluminium electronics panel; also a toggle switch for operation and calibration, input gain, output level, phase, low cut. Modelled: all eight connectors. Not stated: the XLR genders (convention: inputs female, outputs male), the network connector (RJ45 assumed) and the mains inlet (iec-c14 assumed): the plan row carries assumedConnectors net and power-in, both non-audio ports. The BNC pair is AES3 on 75 ohm BNC (aes3 signal). The page does not say the cabinet is rounded (radius 8 mm is our estimate). The `power` switch is the simulator power control, not the page's toggle. Positions are guesses."
    }
